        "id": "ch6_2-1",
        "text": "Understanding devices in Linux\nAs already stated on several occasions in this book, everything in Linux is a file. This also includes\ndevices. Device files are special files in Unix and Linux operating systems. Those special files are\ninterfaces to device drivers, and they are present in the filesystem as a regular file.\nWith no further ado, let\u2019s see how Linux abstraction layers work. This will give you an overview of\nhow hardware and software are related and interconnected.\nWorking with Disks and Filesystems\n188\nEsta secci\u00f3n contiene las siguientes subsecciones\n\u2022 Linux abstraction layers\n\u2022 Device files and naming conventions\nSi deseas explorar cualquiera de estas subsecciones, puedes pregunt\u00e1rmelo directamente.",
